; The example programs, as a library the suites can build worlds from.
;
; examples/ is one complete program per step of the guide, ending in the
; `let () =` that opens a window. Nothing there changes to be tested: each
; source is copied here with that last binding cut off, which leaves exactly
; the definitions above it — the materials, the components and the level.
;
; The bug this exists for lived in examples/ for twenty-one files precisely
; because nothing built these worlds. test_examples does now.

(rule
 (target step01_room.ml)
 (deps %{project_root}/examples/step01_room.ml)
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   %{target}
   (run awk "/^let \\(\\) =/{exit}{print}" %{deps}))))

